* CURSES.INS — udt_curses BASIC API.  Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.
* GPL-2.0-only.  $INCLUDE this at the top of a program to use the bridge.
*
*   $INCLUDE BP CURSES.INS
*
* ---- availability -----------------------------------------------------
* Always safe to call, whether or not the bridge is installed:
   DEFFUN CALLC.EXISTS(A)
   DEFFUN CURSES.AVAIL(A)
*
* ---- native entry points (CallC) --------------------------------------
* These are only safe to call once CURSES.AVAIL() has returned 1.  Each
* takes exactly one string argument (ignored where noted) and returns a
* string.  Call them directly, e.g.  K = CALLC CURSKEY("")
*
*   CALLC CURSINIT("")        enter curses mode (raw keys, no echo, mouse)
*   CALLC CURSEND("")         leave curses mode, restore the terminal
*   CALLC CURSDIM("")         "rows cols" of the screen
*   CALLC CURSCURSOR("0")     cursor visibility: "0" hide, "1" normal
*   CALLC CURSCOLOR(spec)     set text colour (see below); like MVX COLOR()
*   CALLC CURSBKGD(spec)      set the screen background (back-colour-erase)
*   CALLC CURSMOVE("r c")     move the cursor (0-based row/col)
*   CALLC CURSADDSTR(text)    write text at the cursor
*   CALLC CURSCLEAR("")       clear the screen (shown at next refresh)
*   CALLC CURSCLREOL("")      clear from the cursor to end of line
*   CALLC CURSREFRESH("")     flush output to the terminal
*   CALLC CURSTIMEOUT("ms")   read timeout for CURSKEY; "-1" blocks
*   CALLC CURSKEY("")         one keystroke as a logical NAME (see below)
*   CALLC CURSMOUSE("")       last mouse event:
*                               col : @VM : row : @VM : button : @VM : event
*                             button LEFT/MIDDLE/RIGHT/NONE, event as below
*
* ---- colour spec (CURSCOLOR / CURSBKGD) -------------------------------
* A colour name, optionally a background, optionally BRIGHT:
*   "GREEN"   "WHITE BLUE" (fg bg)   "BRIGHT GREEN"   "BLACK CYAN"   "OFF"
* Colours: BLACK RED GREEN YELLOW BLUE MAGENTA CYAN WHITE.  "OFF" resets.
*
* ---- key names returned by CURSKEY ------------------------------------
* Printable characters return as themselves.  Named keys, matching MVX's
* KEYIN():
*   UP DOWN LEFT RIGHT  HOME END  PGUP PGDN  INS DEL  BS  TAB BTAB
*   ENTER  ESC  F1..F12  MOUSE
* An empty return means no key within the timeout.  "MOUSE" means a mouse
* event arrived; read it with CURSMOUSE.  Its event field is one of
* DOWN UP DRAG CLICK MOVE WHEELUP WHEELDN.
   EQU CURSES.VM TO CHAR(253)
